## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design data lineage and prompt hygiene features in a practical, beginner-friendly manner. It evaluates understanding of per-tenant privacy requirements and the ability to translate abstract privacy needs into concrete models and tests without requiring knowledge of large-scale system design.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant provenance tracking (input, output, model version)
- Simple redaction policy for PII detection and handling during ingestion and storage
- Lightweight policy schema and data model design
- Minimal test plan with concrete PII examples
- Data residency considerations and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal data lineage model
type LineageRecord = {
  tenantId: string;
  requestId: string;
  timestamp: Date;
  input: {
    prompt: string;
    redactedPrompt?: string;
    tokens: number;
  };
  output?: {
    response: string;
    redactedResponse?: string;
    tokens: number;
  };
  model: {
    provider: string;
    version: string;
  };
};

// Simple redaction policy
const redactionPolicy = {
  patterns: [
    { type: 'EMAIL', regex: /\b[\w.-]+@[\w.-]+\.\w+\b/g },
    { type: 'PHONE', regex: /\b\d{3}[-.]?\d{3}[-.]?\d{4}\b/g },
    { type: 'SSN', regex: /\b\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}\b/g },
  ],
  replacement: '[REDACTED]',
};

function redactPII(text: string): string {
  let redacted = text;
  for (const { regex } of redactionPolicy.patterns) {
    redacted = redacted.replace(regex, redactionPolicy.replacement);
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical QoS, tenant isolation, and rate-limiting design in llm-ops pipelines, focusing on observable behavior under bursty traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Token bucket rate limiting per tenant
- Burst handling and graceful degradation
- Observability: per-tenant latency, token burn, retry metrics
- SLA verification and alerting during bursts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal token bucket for per-tenant pacing
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(ratePerSec, capacity) {
    this.rate = ratePerSec;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  tryAcquire() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.last = now;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    if (this.tokens >= 1) {
      this.tokens -= 1;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

